<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nabu-mukin-zeri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 731–729 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> · Also known as Nabu-mukin-zeri of Bit-Amukani, Mukin-zeri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nabu-mukin-zeri was a chief of the Chaldean tribe of Bit-Amukani who seized the throne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> in 731 BCE after a period of turmoil following the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabonassar">Nabonassar</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiglath-pileser-iii">Tiglath-pileser III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> campaigned against him, besieged his tribal centre of Sapia and by 729 BCE had overthrown him and taken the Babylonian throne himself.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nabu-mukin-zeri.jpg" alt="Nabu-mukin-zeri" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A. T. Clay · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MLC_1805.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
